# ---- Coach challenges (src/ui/ui_coach.cpp; the coach's spoken lines are in assets/coach/speech/<lang>/challenge.lang)
# The tabs of the Coach page: games with the coach, and short sets of positions to solve
coach.tab.training = Training
coach.tab.challenges = Challenges
# Group headings of the list (capitals: section headings)
challenge.group.mates = CHECKMATES
challenge.group.tactics = TACTICS
challenge.group.defence = DEFENCE
challenge.group.endgames = ENDGAMES
# Each challenge (assets/coach/challenges/challenges.txt): a name, a one-line description (about 60
# characters) and a paragraph for the column of the selected challenge
challenge.mate1.name = Mate in one
challenge.mate1.desc = One move, and it's checkmate.
challenge.mate1.detail = Look at every check first: one of them leaves the king no square, no block and no capture.
challenge.mate2.name = Mate in two
challenge.mate2.desc = A move that leaves no defence, then mate.
challenge.mate2.detail = The first move is often a check or a sacrifice that takes a square away from the king. The coach defends as well as it can.
challenge.mate3.name = Mate in three
challenge.mate3.desc = Longer forcing lines.
challenge.mate3.detail = Checks, captures and threats, three moves deep. Calculate the coach's best answer at each step before you touch a piece.
challenge.backrank.name = Back-rank mates
challenge.backrank.desc = A king trapped behind its own pawns.
challenge.backrank.detail = When the pawns in front of a castled king have not moved, a rook or a queen on the last rank can be checkmate. Remove or distract the defenders first.
challenge.patterns.name = Mating patterns
challenge.patterns.desc = Smothered mate, Anastasia, Arabian and other classics.
challenge.patterns.detail = Famous mating nets that come back again and again. Learn to recognise the pieces' set-up and the final blow.
challenge.hanging.name = Free pieces
challenge.hanging.desc = Spot what is left unprotected.
challenge.hanging.detail = A piece or a pawn that nobody defends can simply be taken. Check what each of the coach's pieces is guarded by.
challenge.fork.name = Forks
challenge.fork.desc = One piece attacks two at once.
challenge.fork.detail = Knights, pawns, queens and even kings can fork. The opponent can only save one of the two targets.
challenge.pin.name = Pins
challenge.pin.desc = A piece that cannot move without losing what stands behind it.
challenge.pin.detail = Pin a piece to its king or to a more valuable piece, then attack it again, or use the fact that it cannot move.
challenge.skewer.name = Skewers
challenge.skewer.desc = Attack a valuable piece and win the one behind it.
challenge.skewer.detail = The reverse of a pin: the more valuable piece stands in front, must move away, and uncovers the piece behind it.
challenge.discovered.name = Discovered attacks
challenge.discovered.desc = Move one piece to unleash another.
challenge.discovered.detail = When a piece steps out of a line, the piece behind it attacks. With check, or with a double check, the opponent has no time to answer both threats.
challenge.deflection.name = Deflection and decoy
challenge.deflection.desc = Lure a defender away, or onto a fatal square.
challenge.deflection.detail = A defender that has two jobs cannot do both. Attack it, offer it something, or force a piece onto the square where it will be lost.
challenge.intermezzo.name = In-between moves
challenge.intermezzo.desc = Don't recapture at once: there is something stronger.
challenge.intermezzo.detail = Before the expected move, a check or a bigger threat in between changes everything.
challenge.trapped.name = Trapped pieces
challenge.trapped.desc = A piece with no safe square left.
challenge.trapped.detail = Take away the last escape squares of a piece, then win it.
challenge.promotion.name = Promotion
challenge.promotion.desc = Push a pawn through to the last rank.
challenge.promotion.detail = Advanced pawns are worth a lot. Clear the way, deflect the blockers, and make a new queen.
challenge.quiet.name = Quiet moves
challenge.quiet.desc = The winning move is neither a check nor a capture.
challenge.quiet.detail = Sometimes the strongest move just prepares a threat that cannot be parried. The hardest kind to see.
challenge.opening.name = Opening traps
challenge.opening.desc = Punish early mistakes.
challenge.opening.detail = Positions from the first moves of real games, where one careless move can be exploited at once.
challenge.escape.name = Find the escape
challenge.escape.desc = Your king is in danger: one move saves it.
challenge.escape.detail = Every other move loses. Look at all the checks and threats against your king, then find the only way out.
challenge.defend.name = Defensive moves
challenge.defend.desc = Parry the threat without losing material.
challenge.defend.detail = The coach threatens something. Find the precise move that keeps everything together.
challenge.kq.name = Queen and king against king
challenge.kq.desc = Checkmate with the queen.
challenge.kq.detail = Push the lone king to the edge with your queen, bring your own king closer, and beware of stalemate. The coach defends with its best moves.
challenge.kr.name = Rook and king against king
challenge.kr.desc = Checkmate with the rook.
challenge.kr.detail = The rook cuts the king off, rank by rank; your king takes the opposition. The coach defends with its best moves.
challenge.kp.name = King and pawn against king
challenge.kp.desc = Win the opposition and promote.
challenge.kp.detail = Lead with your king, not the pawn. Take the opposition and make a queen that the coach cannot catch.
challenge.kp_hold.name = Stop the pawn
challenge.kp_hold.desc = A lone king against king and pawn: hold the draw.
challenge.kp_hold.detail = Stand in front of the pawn and keep the opposition. Hold for ten moves.
challenge.rook.name = Rook endgames
challenge.rook.desc = The Lucena bridge and the Philidor defence.
challenge.rook.detail = The two positions every player should know: how to win with a pawn on the seventh rank, and how to defend with the rook on the third.
challenge.endgame.name = Endgame tactics
challenge.endgame.desc = Few pieces, sharp ideas.
challenge.endgame.detail = Pawn races, breakthroughs and rook endgames from real games.
